WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.036
-My first guest
is a nine-time Emmy nominated

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.403
actor and producer

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:07.507
starring on the seventh season
of "Black-ish,"

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:11.610
which airs Wednesdays
at 9:30 p.m. on ABC.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.381
Here is Anthony Anderson!

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:17.350
Yeah! That --
-Whoo-whoo! Yeah-yeah!

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.318
-Yeah, the neat-looking.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:21.187
You look good, buddy.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.388
I love it.
-Thank you, baby.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:23.556
-You look great, man.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.559
Thanks for coming back
on the show.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.061
Hey, how was your
Halloween weekend?

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.996
Did you celebrate Halloween?

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:31.865
-No, I did not celebrate it,
man.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.900
You know, our kids
are 24 and 20 now,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.069
and they're out of the house.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:40.840
So there was really no need
for us to celebrate Halloween.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.376
But my wife wanted to decorate.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.211
And I was like,
"Okay, that's cool."

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:48.014
But she decorated the house,
man, inside and out

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.283
as if we were having kids
come up to the door.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:53.219
And I was like, I don't want
these little COVID babies

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.721
running up to our door,

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.223
ringing the doorbell,
trying to get candy.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:00.193
-Yeah. I want no people
to come here.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:03.896
-No, we normally do it big on
Halloween in our neighborhood,

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:06.065
but, you know, no one did.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:08.968
But she decorated
the inside of the house

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:12.305
like it was
a Halloween festival, man.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:15.975
And it's just her, myself,
and our blind dog Riley

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:19.679
just walking around bumping into
pumpkins and candy stashes.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.680
And I'm a type 2 diabetic,
Jimmy.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:22.982
So I don't know why
she's tempting me

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.084
with all this damn candy
in the house.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.652
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:28.454
I want to talk to you --

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.890
Last time I talked to you,
you were planning on

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.759
all these big summer
celebrations

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.994
you were looking forward to,

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.229
but with quarantine,
you can't really do that.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:39.065
I mean, you were
going to get your star

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:40.533
on the Hollywood Walk of Fame,

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.535
and you were going to turn 50.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.772
-I did.
Those things still happened.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:48.641
They just didn't happen
like we wanted them to.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.343
There was no pomp
and circumstance

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.612
for the star
on the Walk of Fame.

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:58.084
I had 11 people there --
8 family members,

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:03.256
my manager who spoke,
my agent, and George Lopez,

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:07.527
who spoke at --
and my mom, who spoke, as well.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:10.763
Oh, I would be remiss
if I didn't show you this.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.899
Let me see -- Can you see that?
-Yeah.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.668
-It's my Hollywood
Walk of Fame ring...

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.403
-Wow.
-...that George Lopez

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.738
and Ced the Entertainer
got for me.

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:22.708
-Holy moly. That's a nice ring.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:26.345
Wait. Why do they -- Why -- Just
'cause they're your friends?

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:30.183
-Yeah, well, George Lopez got
his star on the Walk of Fame.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.218
He was the first one
of our whole crew.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.521
So he bought the ring
for himself.

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:37.690
Cedric the Entertainer was the
next one of our crew who got it,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.359
so he bought Ced a ring.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:40.926
I was the third in our crew,

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:45.097
so George and Ced
put in and got the ring.

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:49.168
And our crew is me, George,
Ced, D.L. Hughley,

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.503
Don Cheadle, and Chris Spencer.

00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:54.740
So, the next person who --
who I believe is Don

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.376
who's next in line,
we'll all pitch in

00:02:57.376 --> 00:03:00.847
and get him his Hollywood
Walk of Fame ring, as well.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:04.484
-I saw a fun video that
you posted of you and your son

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:06.886
celebrating your star
on the Walk of Fame.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.422
Let's take a look at
a little bit of that right here.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.824 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.759
[ Laughs ]

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:15.528
Come on, dude.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.731
-[ Laughs ]
-Come on, dude.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.834
-I don't think
that's the song that was playing

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.904
when we were dancing
on the strip, there, Jimmy.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.706
-We couldn't clear that song.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.541
-No, I understand. I understand.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.909
I just want the world to know

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.178
that's not what was playing
from the car.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.713
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:37.383
-We can't afford that, man.
Come on.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.918
That's a dream come true, man.
That's pretty cool.

00:03:39.918 --> 00:03:42.522
You have a star
on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:45.724
-Yeah, man, it is.
And I went to Hollywood High,

00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:49.829
literally across the street
from where my star is.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.097
And never in a thousand years
did I ever think

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:55.368
walking those streets
that I would be immortalized

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.904
on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.
-Oh, congrats.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.305
-And I want
to throw this in there.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.942
My mother has vowed to come
out there with her assistant

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.645
once a month to clean my star.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:09.382
Mama, November 5th
is your month.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.317
Come up. It's your day
of the month,

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.751
November 5th.
-Oh, my God. Do not --

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:14.853
-The 5th of every month,
she has to come out.

00:04:14.853 --> 00:04:17.489
-No, do not make your mom
clean your -- Absolutely not.

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:19.392
No, no. You're a big boy.
-She offered it, Jimmy!

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:20.560
She offered it!
-You're a big boy now.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.227
You don't do that. Come on, man.

00:04:22.227 --> 00:04:24.063
You're 50.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.397
-Yeah.
-That's amazing.

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:27.566
You look fantastic.
50 years old.

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:29.168
-Thank you, babe. Well, you know
black don't crack.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.570
It does chip
a little bit, though,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.405
and it starts to rot
on the inside.

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:36.008
-Wait, I have to talk
about this.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:38.644
You did something
very big recently,

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.646
I think like around
two weeks ago

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:42.614
that was --
-Oh.

00:04:42.614 --> 00:04:43.949
[ Laughs ]

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:45.752
-I have to talk about it.
Can we?

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.053
-Yeah, let's talk about it.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.988
You know what? I went and had --

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:52.258
Because I turned 50, I went
and had a colonoscopy done.

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.793
It was that time.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:57.230
-You know, I had been getting
the PSA, the blood test done

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.331
up until then. But turning 50 --

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:03.169
And I should actually had this
procedure done when I was 45,

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.670
so I'm a little late
to the game.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.272
But I wanted to document it

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:09.642
to take the stigma
off of getting a colonoscopy,

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:15.114
especially for men of color, to
go in and get this checked out,

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.415
because it's better --
-What is it like?

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:19.852
What do you do?
What is it like?

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.020
-You know what, man?
They give you --

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.189
You change your diet
four to five days before,

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.825
and it's a low-fiber diet
for obvious reasons.

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.259
-Yeah.

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:29.728
-The prep day
is the most difficult day,

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:31.998
and difficult is the only word
that I can use

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.632
be-- It's not that bad.

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:35.467
You have to flush yourself out.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.536
They give you
a solution to drink.

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:39.572
You can't eat any solid foods.

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:43.108
And you go into the doctor's
office the next day,

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:44.710
they give you
the Michael Jackson,

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.246
you lay it out
for an hour and a half,

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:51.517
and you don't feel anything
before, during, or after.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.552
-You don't.
And so you're back up,

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:55.621
and you're like,
everything went well?

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:58.991
-It was best hour and a half
nap, sleep that I had.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:03.262
The procedure
only took 15 minutes.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:06.765
And as I posted
on my social media pages,

00:06:06.765 --> 00:06:08.801
I had a clean bill of health.
-[ Clapping ]

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:11.938
-You know, there were no polyps.
There was nothing there.

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:16.442
So I did that so I could get
men, especially men of color,

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:20.946
to go into their doctor's office
and get a colonoscopy done.

00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:24.349
It's better
to have it done early

00:06:24.349 --> 00:06:27.453
and understand what it is
that you need done

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:30.756
if you need something done
than wait till the last minute,

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:33.225
and the outcome
won't be so great.

00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:34.559
-It's great that you did that,
and it's great

00:06:34.559 --> 00:06:36.929
that you're using your platform
to raise awareness.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.664
There's a lot more
to talk about.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.566
Can you stick around
for a little longer?

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:43.101
-I have nowhere to go, Jimmy.

00:06:43.101 --> 00:06:45.071
-More with Anthony Anderson
when we come back.

